*> Implementation test of proto/src/buffer.cob (contracts/proto-api.md §1): PB-INIT capacity,
*> PB-APPEND-BYTES growth beyond the capacity, PB-RESET, PB-FREE, PB-GET-BYTES and PB-SKIP past
*> PB-LENGTH set PB-ERROR and leave PB-POS, and the error stays set until PB-RESET.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-BUFFER.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BYTES               PIC X(200).
 01 WS-OUT                 PIC X(200).
 01 WS-HEX                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-PTR                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NUM                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE 100 TO WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     MOVE "test buffer PB-INIT 100 gives capacity 100, length 0, pos 0, no error" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "100 0 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE "test buffer PB-FREE releases the memory (address NULL, capacity 0)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF PB-ADDR = NULL AND PB-CAPACITY = 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     MOVE "test buffer PB-INIT 0 allocates the minimum of 16 bytes" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "16 0 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT
*>   Growth: 10 bytes fit; 20 more exceed 16 and double to 32; 100 more need 130 (more than double).
     MOVE ALL "a" TO WS-BYTES(1:10)
     MOVE ALL "b" TO WS-BYTES(11:20)
     MOVE ALL "c" TO WS-BYTES(31:100)
     MOVE 10 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES(1:10) WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test buffer PB-APPEND-BYTES of 10 bytes keeps capacity 16" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "16 10 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT
     MOVE 20 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES(11:20) WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test buffer PB-APPEND-BYTES beyond the capacity doubles it to 32" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "32 30 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT
     MOVE 100 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES(31:100) WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test buffer PB-APPEND-BYTES needing more than double grows to the exact size 130"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "130 130 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES WS-COUNT
     MOVE 130 TO WS-COUNT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OUT
     CALL "PB-GET-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-OUT WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test buffer bytes survive both moves to new memory" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-BYTES(1:130) TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-OUT(1:130) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Reads past PB-LENGTH.
     MOVE 125 TO PB-POS
     MOVE 6 TO WS-COUNT
     MOVE ALL "x" TO WS-OUT
     CALL "PB-GET-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-OUT WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test buffer PB-GET-BYTES past PB-LENGTH sets PB-ERROR, keeps PB-POS, yields zeros"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "130 130 125 1 000000000000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT-START
     STRING " " FUNCTION HEX-OF(WS-OUT(1:6)) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
         WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "PB-GET-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-OUT WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test buffer PB-GET-BYTES after an error yields zeros even when data remains" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "130 130 125 1 00" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT-START
     STRING " " FUNCTION HEX-OF(WS-OUT(1:1)) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
         WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "PB-SKIP" USING PB-BUFFER WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test buffer PB-SKIP after an error keeps PB-POS" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "130 130 125 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE "test buffer PB-RESET empties the buffer, clears PB-ERROR, keeps the memory" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "130 0 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT
     MOVE 5 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTES WS-COUNT
     MOVE 3 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "PB-SKIP" USING PB-BUFFER WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test buffer PB-SKIP 3 of 5 bytes advances PB-POS" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "130 5 3 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT
     MOVE 3 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "PB-SKIP" USING PB-BUFFER WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test buffer PB-SKIP past PB-LENGTH sets PB-ERROR and keeps PB-POS" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "130 5 3 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE -1 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "PB-SKIP" USING PB-BUFFER WS-COUNT
     MOVE "test buffer PB-SKIP of a negative count sets PB-ERROR" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "130 0 0 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     STOP RUN.

*> TL-EXPECTED against "capacity length pos error".
 STATE-TEXT.
     PERFORM STATE-TEXT-START
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

 STATE-TEXT-START.
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     MOVE PB-CAPACITY TO WS-NUM
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE PB-LENGTH TO WS-NUM
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE PB-POS TO WS-NUM
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-NUM
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER.

 ADD-NUMBER.
     MOVE WS-NUM TO WS-EDIT
     IF WS-PTR > 1
         STRING " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     END-IF
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR.
 END PROGRAM TEST-BUFFER.
